     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. 9,000 mg/day of acetaminophen is more than double the 4,000 mg/day maximum. It is in the range associated with acute liver injury, and normal liver function doesn't protect against that. I can't think of an indication that would make it safe.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a standard regimen right away.** For example, 1000 mg PO three times daily (3,000 mg/day), or 1000 mg PO four times daily (4,000 mg/day) if you want the maximum.\n- **Help you reassess the plan.** If the goal is stronger analgesia or fever control, I can enter a multimodal regimen with other agents, which you would specify.\n- **Check for a typo.** If you meant 300 mg or 1000 mg per dose, tell me and I'll enter it.\n\nIf you have an unusual reason for this dose, please talk to pharmacy or your attending first. It should go through your institution's high-dose override process, not a standard order entry.\n\nWhich option would you like?"
      }
